  "raw": " XC40 is, as far as tech goes, the way to go serious about EV adoption. And Volvo has its facts straight on how long it took for absolute EV dominance of the auto industry — notably because of Nissan’s and Callahan‘s Leaf, which came out in 2007.)\nOther manufacturers aren’t waiting, either: today Ford announced some big moves worldwide, some retail and L1 vehicle news too, but they all point to going electric sooner rather than later. It now looks like mainstream automakers will start acting upon this reality from earlier….\nNext big wave inundating every industry globally begins in 2016 or so, with CVVs delivering them online before any battery-based products. Or functionally equivalent large mass market EV pickups/SUV trucks are coming a lot sooner though. Again, batteries will drive sales volume markedly higher even if no pure EVs yet available; huge lead… valued brands should be paying real carriers/pubishments handsomely for huge ad plac",
